{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6snqxj4vz7jyprs75znakhuosi35isghq4kxep5b6eakkkvnmz3a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The translation is complete and verified.\n\n## What the C library is\n\n`c_src/` is a single-file library: `src/driver.c` + `include/driver.h`, built by CMake as one shared lib. Its entire public ABI is **one symbol**:\n\n```\n$ nm -D --defined-only libdriver.so   →   driver\n```\n\n`void driver(int x, int y)` — a `while` loop with two labels and backward/forward `goto`s (`goto label2` skips the `x` block; `goto label1` is a *backward* jump inside the same iteration, so the body is effectively an inner loop that does **not** re-check the `while` condition).\n\n## Rust translation (`translation/`)\n\n- `Cargo.toml`: `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`.\n- `src/lib.rs`: `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub extern \"C\" fn driver(x: c_int, y: c_int)`, signature preserved via `std::ffi`. No namespace/rename macros exist in the header, so the linker name is plain `driver`.\n- Control flow reproduced exactly with an outer `'while_loop` + inner `loop` (the inner `continue` is `goto label1`, `break` is fall-through to the condition, `continue 'while_loop` is the C `continue`), plus a `skip_label1` flag for `goto label2`.\n- Output goes through the **real libc `printf`** (declared `extern \"C\"`), so stdout buffering/byte stream matches the C library exactly.\n- Decrements use `wrapping_sub` to mirror the C code's wrap-around behavior on the pathological inputs (e.g. `x>0, y<0` runs ~2³¹ iterations) instead of panicking — no bug fixes, no behavior changes.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo build --release` — clean, no warnings.\n- **Symbol gate:** `nm -D --defined-only` diff between the C `.so` and the Rust `.so` is **empty in both directions** (`driver` ↔ `driver`).\n- **Differential testing** against the compiled C library via identical harnesses linked to each `.so`:\n  - all 1147 terminating inputs `x ∈ [-6,30] × y ∈ [0,30]`: byte-identical stdout + identical exit codes, 0 mismatches;\n  - non-terminating inputs (`x>0, y<0`, plus `INT_MAX` cases): first 300–500 KB of output byte-identical;\n  - edge cases (`0/0`, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, the `x==1 && y==4` `goto label2` path, large values): all identical.\n\nOne note: `rm -rf` is blocked by the sandbox, so my scratch test directory `_diff/` (a copy of the C build + harness binaries) is still in the working root — `c_src/` itself was never modified. Feel free to delete `_diff/`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":759,"cache_read_input_tokens":38497,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":759,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0a9923d0-6750-49f2-809d-c7f48b6bd684","uuid":"1b8ab623-ec50-46e8-9a8b-91e35a3e3bb2","timestamp":"2026-08-28T13:49:26.045Z"}
